  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1d462-p51-practice-slot-11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Write an equation of a line that is parallel to $3x-2y=8$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $y=\\frac32x$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3x-2y&=8\\\\-2y&=8-3x\\\\y&=\\frac32x-4\\end{align*}$$\nThe gradient is $\\frac32$. A parallel line has the same gradient and a different $y$-intercept; for example, $y=\\frac32x$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
